# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# net-cni: overlay-CNI pod networking for the kube-node guest.
#
# ch-guest-k8s is a Kubernetes node running the container stack INSIDE a Cloud
# Hypervisor guest.  layer-containers gives it service networking (IPVS) and
# the veth/bridge/nftables plumbing, but a pod overlay needs the encap devices
# themselves -- and those live in layer-hypervisor (a metal-host concern) that
# a guest never merges.  Without them this SKU ships BRIDGE/VETH/IP_VS only and
# cannot bring up an overlay CNI at all.
#
# Scope (deliberate): the three encaps that cover the CNIs we support, plus an
# encrypted mesh.
#   VXLAN    -- flannel (default), Calico VXLAN mode, Cilium VXLAN tunnel.
#   GENEVE   -- Cilium's default tunnel, OVN-Kubernetes.
#   WIREGUARD -- Cilium / Calico transparent node-to-node pod encryption.
#   MACVLAN / IPVLAN -- the CNI plugins of the same name (and Multus subnets).
#
# Applied via the ch-guest-k8s profile's OVERRIDES -- k8s-only.  It is NOT in
# plain ch-guest: a sold/first-party VM is not a pod host and gains no overlay
# encap or an always-resident WireGuard crypto core it never uses.
#
# Guests are MONOLITHIC (CONFIG_MODULES is off), so every symbol is =y; there
# is no module to load an overlay driver on demand.
#
# WireGuard's crypto is NOT listed here on purpose.  In this kernel WIREGUARD
# `select`s the invisible library primitives it uses directly --
# CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519, CRYPTO_LIB_CHACHA20POLY1305, CRYPTO_LIB_UTILS (plus
# NET_UDP_TUNNEL / DST_CACHE) -- so =y forces them on with no explicit line,
# exactly as VXLAN/GENEVE pull NET_UDP_TUNNEL/GRO_CELLS.  These are the library
# primitives, NOT the crypto-API CRYPTO_CHACHA20POLY1305 / CRYPTO_CURVE25519
# transforms, which WireGuard does not use.  check-config confirms WIREGUARD=y
# survives resolution; adding the invisible selects by hand would only restate
# what the Kconfig already guarantees (and matches how layer-hypervisor lists
# these same encaps without their selects).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_VXLAN=y
CONFIG_GENEVE=y
CONFIG_MACVLAN=y
CONFIG_IPVLAN=y
CONFIG_WIREGUARD=y
